{
 "android-navigation|Tabs and segmented buttons": {
  "summary": "Plenix tabs and segmented buttons on Android are Material 3’s tabs and segmented buttons, kept native in behavior (swiping between tab pages, scrollable tab rows, single or multiple selection, ripple, TalkBack tab and selection semantics, font scaling) and styled with the Plenix tokens: tabs on the default surface with DM Sans labels in the label role, the selected tab in the default content color and semibold over an indicator in the selected color, and segmented buttons on the neutral fill with the 6 dp control radius, the control border and the selected segment raised. Material’s default colors the selected tab and its indicator in the primary color and fills the selected segment in the secondary container with a check; Plenix keeps Material’s structure and replaces the look.",
  "variants": [
